# {{PROJECT}}

Created with Galadon on {{DATE}} using the `webapp` layout and the
`{{STACK}}` stack.

The engineering loop is:

```text
Spec -> Build -> Verify -> Ship -> Learn
```

Start with:

```bash
galadon next
```

## Layout

```text
server/            backend ({{STACK}})
web/               frontend landing zone; pick the framework here
e2e/               end-to-end tests
tests/             unit tests
openspec/          construction tickets
spec/              product behaviour facts
wiki/              knowledge / progress / runbook
.agents/           agent runtime, gitignored
scripts/dev.sh     run the backend locally (python/node stacks)
config.md          environment and configuration notes
```

With the `python` or `node` stack, `galadon.yaml` already declares real checks,
so `galadon check` is green on a fresh clone; `--stack none` ships no checks and
no `scripts/dev.sh`, and fails the gate. Secrets belong in `.env` or the secret
provider you configure, never in the YAML file.

## Commands

```bash
scripts/dev.sh
galadon next
galadon check
```
